{
  "_doc": "What 'direct' understands (0.24.33): plain-language direction -> seqtool commands, without a connection to Claude. Each intent: 'say' = phrases that mean it (any case; a word also matches its longer forms: 'calm' matches 'calmer'; '{effect}' = an effect name is in the text), 'not' = phrases that rule it out, 'do' = the commands (slots below; a line starting with '?' is left out when one of its slots isn't in the text), 'means' = what it does, in a few words, 'check' = commands that show it took. Slots: {where} the section named ('@#3', with ' --only' for 'the second chorus'), {at} the same without --only, {prop} the props / groups named (one command each), {words} the quoted words, {time} a moment ('at 1:05', '@vocals'), {effect} an effect name (or a word in 'effect_words'), {hi} / {lo} a value for 'more' / 'less' ('a little', 'a lot' change it), {before_vocals} each section before the singing (the one it starts in: until=@vocals), {grow} / {shrink} 'sections move' commands for 'by 2 bars' / 'by 4 beats' / 'by 3 s'; '@WORD' as a time = where that word is sung. '{slot|default}': the default when the text doesn't have it ('yard' = the group holding the most props, '--song' = this song). Mistyped words are put right when they are close to a word it knows (general.fuzzy); 'plain_words' are never taken as typos. Add your own in seqtool-prefs/intents.json under \"intents\" (a new name, or an existing one to change it).",
